# Worker health needs no secrets. /api/tmdb reads these bindings per request.
# Copy to .dev.vars locally; use Worker secrets in Cloudflare.
# MovieGraph Local generates .dev.vars.local and .local.env automatically.
# Keep the TMDB credential here; do not paste Neon URLs for that local workflow.
# Prefer the TMDB read access token; API key remains supported as an alternative.
# TMDB_READ_ACCESS_TOKEN=replace-with-your-tmdb-read-access-token
# TMDB_API_KEY=replace-with-your-tmdb-api-key
# TMDB_BASE_URL=https://api.themoviedb.org/3
# Local database credentials are generated in .local.env; do not put Neon URLs here.
# Remote Workers use Hyperdrive IDs in their Wrangler configs and Cloudflare secrets.
# See docs/ENVIRONMENTS.md. Never put database credentials in VITE_* variables.
